WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.327 --> 00:00:16.767
Stand aside. you. Make way.

2
00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:19.367
Clear a path.

3
00:00:19.447 --> 00:00:23.567
Come on. get back. Out of the way!

4
00:00:37.087 --> 00:00:42.527
I need another oarsman
for my barge. a strong slave.

5
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.167
- Your word is our will.
- The large one there.

6
00:00:46.207 --> 00:00:47.247
You!

7
00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:51.847
No. not that one.
The very dirty one there.

8
00:00:51.927 --> 00:00:56.447
Yes. that one.
He may serve my purpose.

9
00:00:56.527 --> 00:00:57.967
You!

10
00:00:58.007 --> 00:00:59.887
YOU!

11
00:00:59.927 --> 00:01:02.447
Out of the pit!

12
00:01:06.647 --> 00:01:10.847
Out of the way! Back to work!

13
00:01:10.887 --> 00:01:13.607
Clear a path!

14
00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:17.727
Back to work!

15
00:01:21.687 --> 00:01:26.767
First friend of the Pharaoh.
keeper of the royal seal.

16
00:01:26.807 --> 00:01:32.207
Prince of Memphis.
Prince of Thebes.

17
00:01:32.247 --> 00:01:37.007
beloved of the Nile god.
conqueror of Ethiopia.

18
00:01:37.087 --> 00:01:39.807
general of generals.

19
00:01:39.847 --> 00:01:42.607
commander of the Egyptian Host.

20
00:01:42.647 --> 00:01:45.167
and man of mud!

21
00:01:46.407 --> 00:01:50.767
Is that what you want? To be a slave?

22
00:01:50.807 --> 00:01:55.567
Then why aren't you kneeling
at the feet of a princess?

23
00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:59.327
I'm afraid the mud pits have
stiffened my knees. royal one.

24
00:02:00.327 --> 00:02:03.007
Shall I call back the guards?

25
00:02:03.047 --> 00:02:07.647
- Do you think they could bend them?
- Oh. Moses! Moses!

26
00:02:07.687 --> 00:02:11.687
You stubborn. splendid.
adorable fool.

27
00:02:16.647 --> 00:02:19.607
I'm not kneeling to a princess.

28
00:02:19.687 --> 00:02:22.527
No. You are kneeling to a woman

29
00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:27.087
who's been worried about you
day and night since you disappeared.

30
00:02:27.127 --> 00:02:32.247
What is there in the mud pits
that could keep you from my arms?

31
00:02:32.287 --> 00:02:34.087
My people.

32
00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:39.087
Do you have to wallow
with your people? Smell like them?

33
00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:43.047
If they are stained.
it's with the mud of slavery.

34
00:02:43.087 --> 00:02:46.527
If they reek.
it's with the stench of injustice.

35
00:02:46.607 --> 00:02:52.047
- Come back to the palace.
- And hide the truth from Sethi?

36
00:02:52.127 --> 00:02:54.847
That I am Hebrew and a slave.

37
00:02:54.887 --> 00:02:57.767
The truth would break
his dear old heart

38
00:02:57.847 --> 00:03:01.687
and send Bithiah
into exile or death.

39
00:03:01.727 --> 00:03:04.167
Stop hearing the cries
of your people.

40
00:03:04.247 --> 00:03:06.767
Their god does not hear their cry.

41
00:03:06.807 --> 00:03:10.807
Will Rameses hear it
if he is Pharaoh?

42
00:03:10.847 --> 00:03:15.047
No. He would grind them
into the clay they mould.

43
00:03:15.087 --> 00:03:17.847
double their labours.

44
00:03:17.887 --> 00:03:21.887
What about me?
Think of me as his wife.

45
00:03:24.407 --> 00:03:27.527
Do you want to see me
in Rameses' arms?

46
00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:29.127
No.

47
00:03:29.207 --> 00:03:31.807
Then come back with me.

48
00:03:31.847 --> 00:03:36.367
Oh. Moses! The gods have
fashioned you for greatness.

49
00:03:36.447 --> 00:03:40.967
The splendour of your name
will last beyond the pyramids.

50
00:03:41.007 --> 00:03:46.327
As Pharaoh. you can free your people.
worship whatever gods you please.

51
00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:49.727
so long as I can worship you.

52
00:04:01.527 --> 00:04:06.047
I will come to you at the palace
on the day of Sethi's jubilee.

53
00:04:06.087 --> 00:04:08.047
Come with me now.

54
00:04:10.607 --> 00:04:12.167
No. my love.

55
00:04:12.247 --> 00:04:17.007
First I have a call to make
on the master builder.

56
00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.767
No. no. no. no. no.

57
00:04:35.807 --> 00:04:38.407
Not red with the samil gown.

58
00:04:45.287 --> 00:04:49.647
My eyes can best be used
elsewhere. Lord Baka.

59
00:04:49.727 --> 00:04:54.647
Before you go. let them look
upon what you thought unworthy.

60
00:04:54.687 --> 00:04:58.687
Who would let beauty
such as this go unseen?

61
00:04:58.727 --> 00:05:02.727
Who would let such a flower
go ungathered?

62
00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:09.207
Dathan. you can see only mud.
so pick up her muddy clothes and go.

63
00:05:10.207 --> 00:05:12.167
Go. all of you.

64
00:05:14.967 --> 00:05:19.967
Did you know that this golden web was
spun from the beards of shellfish?

65
00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:25.887
- Please let me go to my home.
- You ARE at home.

66
00:05:25.927 --> 00:05:28.807
Here. taste this.

67
00:05:28.847 --> 00:05:32.287
The blood of Thracian grapes.
the wine of love.

68
00:05:32.327 --> 00:05:35.607
No wine can change my love.

69
00:05:37.287 --> 00:05:40.007
Then your love shall be my wine.

70
00:05:40.047 --> 00:05:43.167
There's fire in the chariot house!

71
00:05:43.247 --> 00:05:45.607
The chariot house.

72
00:05:45.647 --> 00:05:49.407
Guards! Guards!
Take water to the roof.

73
00:05:49.487 --> 00:05:52.767
Dathan. take charge.
Guards. after him.

74
00:05:53.327 --> 00:05:55.967
Pull it out of the shed.

75
00:05:56.007 --> 00:05:58.607
Take it clear of the house.

76
00:05:59.687 --> 00:06:06.447
No. your wings must not be singed.
at least not by that fire.

77
00:06:07.527 --> 00:06:10.087
- Joshua!
- Run! The way is clear.

78
00:06:10.127 --> 00:06:13.247
The master builder will not follow.

79
00:06:13.287 --> 00:06:15.887
Neither will you. stonecutter.

80
00:06:26.967 --> 00:06:28.927
Bind him between the columns.

81
00:06:32.687 --> 00:06:36.687
See that his arms
are tightly stretched.

82
00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:41.087
You will die on your feet.
stonecutter.

83
00:06:50.847 --> 00:06:53.527
Now go after the girl.

84
00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:56.847
And don't come back without her.

85
00:06:59.887 --> 00:07:02.607
You foolish. stupid man!

86
00:07:03.847 --> 00:07:07.847
I would have kept her
only a short while.

87
00:07:07.887 --> 00:07:12.647
She would have returned to you -
shall we say - more worthy.

88
00:07:12.727 --> 00:07:15.407
Now to whom shall I return Lilia?

89
00:07:15.447 --> 00:07:18.047
You will not be there. Joshua.

90
00:07:19.087 --> 00:07:22.287
You've seen me drive my chariot.

91
00:07:22.327 --> 00:07:28.327
I can flick a fly from my horse's ear
without breaking his stride.

92
00:07:28.367 --> 00:07:30.927
You've seen me use my whip.

93
00:07:33.887 --> 00:07:36.447
You make no outcry. Joshua.

94
00:07:36.487 --> 00:07:39.007
But you will.

95
00:07:39.047 --> 00:07:41.807
You will cry for the mercy of death.

96
00:07:43.807 --> 00:07:47.687
One day you will listen
to the cry of slaves.

97
00:07:47.727 --> 00:07:50.287
This is not that day. Joshua.

98
00:07:57.447 --> 00:08:01.807
You hold your tongue almost
as well as I hold my temper.

99
00:08:01.887 --> 00:08:05.407
It's a pity to kill
so strong a stonecutter.

100
00:08:06.447 --> 00:08:10.447
- Death will bring death. Baka.
- Who are you?

101
00:08:10.487 --> 00:08:13.527
One who asks
what right you have to kill.

102
00:08:13.567 --> 00:08:16.607
The right of a master
to kill any slave.

103
00:08:17.887 --> 00:08:21.087
- Kill ME. master butcher!
- Moses!

104
00:08:37.727 --> 00:08:39.687
Why have you done this?

105
00:08:39.767 --> 00:08:42.127
- Where is Lilia?
- Gone.

106
00:08:42.207 --> 00:08:45.167
Why are you dressed as a slave?

107
00:08:45.247 --> 00:08:50.407
Why does a prince of Egypt kill
the master builder to save a Hebrew?

108
00:08:52.727 --> 00:08:54.527
I am Hebrew.

109
00:08:59.207 --> 00:09:03.807
God of Abraham.
Four hundred years we've waited.

110
00:09:03.847 --> 00:09:06.527
The Pharaoh's soldiers
won't wait so long.

111
00:09:06.567 --> 00:09:10.087
The Almighty has heard our cries.

112
00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:12.927
You are the chosen one.

113
00:09:12.967 --> 00:09:16.967
- I know nothing of your god.
- He knows YOU.

114
00:09:17.007 --> 00:09:21.847
He has brought you to us.
You cannot turn your back upon us.

115
00:09:21.927 --> 00:09:26.927
You will deliver us. The finger
of God points the way to YOU.

116
00:09:29.727 --> 00:09:35.167
- Where was his body found?
- Buried in the sand. royal one.

117
00:09:36.727 --> 00:09:39.287
This is Baka's knife.

118
00:09:39.327 --> 00:09:41.967
There was no wound on the body.

119
00:09:42.007 --> 00:09:47.007
Baka was a powerful man. It would
take strong hands to break him.

120
00:09:47.087 --> 00:09:49.727
The slave. Joshua. is a stonecutter.

121
00:09:50.727 --> 00:09:53.367
Go find me this Joshua.

122
00:09:55.727 --> 00:09:59.727
Joshua's strength didn't kill
the master builder.

123
00:09:59.767 --> 00:10:03.367
Now speaks the rat
that would be my ears.

124
00:10:03.447 --> 00:10:06.407
Too many ears tie a rat's tongue.

125
00:10:09.727 --> 00:10:12.367
Go. All of you.

126
00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:18.127
Well? Who killed him?

127
00:10:18.207 --> 00:10:23.047
I am a poor man. generous one.
What I bring is worth much.

128
00:10:23.127 --> 00:10:26.567
I have paid you much
and you have brought nothing.

129
00:10:26.607 --> 00:10:31.607
Now I bring the world...
true son of Pharaoh.

130
00:10:31.687 --> 00:10:37.847
You offer me the world when you
cannot even bring me the deliverer.

131
00:10:37.927 --> 00:10:39.967
Who killed Baka?

132
00:10:40.047 --> 00:10:44.127
- The deliverer.
- Would you play at words with me?

133
00:10:44.167 --> 00:10:46.687
No. lord prince.

134
00:10:46.727 --> 00:10:50.567
This murderer has now fled
to some distant land?

135
00:10:50.607 --> 00:10:52.407
No. lord prince.

136
00:10:52.447 --> 00:10:54.247
Name him!

137
00:10:54.287 --> 00:10:57.807
One who made himself
a prince and judge over us.

138
00:10:57.847 --> 00:11:01.367
If he knew I were here.
he would kill me.

139
00:11:02.407 --> 00:11:06.527
I will hang you myself
if you tire me further.

140
00:11:08.887 --> 00:11:13.887
There are those who would pay much
for what my eyes have seen.

141
00:11:13.927 --> 00:11:17.687
You haggle with me
like in a marketplace?

142
00:11:17.727 --> 00:11:21.607
No. I will not haggle.
Here's your money.

143
00:11:23.247 --> 00:11:30.567
But for ten talents of fine gold.
I'll give you the wealth of Egypt.

144
00:11:30.647 --> 00:11:34.327
Give me my freedom
and I'll give you the sceptre.

145
00:11:34.367 --> 00:11:38.647
Give me Lilia and I'll give you
the princess of your heart's desire.

146
00:11:38.727 --> 00:11:42.647
Give me this house
and I'll give you the throne.

147
00:11:42.687 --> 00:11:45.447
Give me all that I ask...

148
00:11:46.727 --> 00:11:49.087
or give me leave to go.

149
00:11:49.167 --> 00:11:52.527
I will give you more
than leave to go.

150
00:11:52.567 --> 00:11:55.207
I will send you where you belong.

151
00:11:55.247 --> 00:11:59.287
I belong in your service.
glorious one.

152
00:12:00.327 --> 00:12:02.527
Very well.

153
00:12:02.607 --> 00:12:05.207
I WILL bargain with you.

154
00:12:06.287 --> 00:12:11.287
If what you say pleases me.
I will give you your price.

155
00:12:11.327 --> 00:12:16.327
If not. I will give you
the point of this blade! Agreed?

156
00:12:16.407 --> 00:12:18.287
Agreed.

157
00:12:18.327 --> 00:12:20.207
The deliverer...

158
00:12:21.287 --> 00:12:23.087
is Moses.

159
00:12:25.727 --> 00:12:30.567
Draw one more breath to tell me why
Moses or any other Egyptian

160
00:12:30.647 --> 00:12:33.007
would deliver the Hebrews?

161
00:12:33.047 --> 00:12:35.487
Moses is not Egyptian.

162
00:12:35.567 --> 00:12:37.367
He's Hebrew.

163
00:12:37.447 --> 00:12:40.047
The son of slaves.

164
00:12:51.247 --> 00:12:53.207
I will pay your price.

165
00:13:21.887 --> 00:13:25.887
I am told. my tiger lily.
they're wagering against me.

166
00:13:25.927 --> 00:13:31.447
- Two golden deber against one.
- Yes. I wagered five myself!

167
00:13:31.487 --> 00:13:34.927
You'll lose if Moses
keeps me waiting any longer.

168
00:13:35.007 --> 00:13:40.207
I double the wager. I'll watch
for Moses. you watch the dance!

169
00:14:03.887 --> 00:14:08.887
While you wait to honour Moses.
I will honour Sethi's jubilee...

170
00:14:11.007 --> 00:14:12.367
with a gift.

171
00:14:12.887 --> 00:14:15.407
Strange gift.

172
00:14:16.767 --> 00:14:20.887
You said if the deliverer
were a myth.

173
00:14:20.927 --> 00:14:24.967
- to bring him in a bottle.
- It is empty.

174
00:14:25.007 --> 00:14:28.687
Yes. Because he is not a myth.

175
00:14:28.727 --> 00:14:32.327
- You have found such a man?
- Yes. Father.

176
00:14:32.367 --> 00:14:35.087
In the midst of treachery
and treason.

177
00:14:35.127 --> 00:14:38.887
with the blood of your
master builder on his hands.

178
00:14:38.927 --> 00:14:42.927
Shall I summon him
to Pharaoh's justice?

179
00:14:42.967 --> 00:14:44.487
Summon him!

180
00:14:49.927 --> 00:14:53.967
- Bring the Hebrew in.
- Bring the Hebrew in.

181
00:15:30.927 --> 00:15:33.487
Great Pharaoh.

182
00:15:33.527 --> 00:15:37.607
I stand in the shadow
of your justice.

183
00:15:37.647 --> 00:15:40.927
Whose work is THIS?

184
00:15:40.967 --> 00:15:43.647
I warned you of his treason.

185
00:15:43.687 --> 00:15:48.207
- Treason?
- Judge now if I spoke truly.

186
00:15:48.287 --> 00:15:50.327
The evil star foretold him

187
00:15:50.407 --> 00:15:54.607
as the destroyer of Egypt
and deliverer of slaves.

188
00:15:54.687 --> 00:15:59.287
It is not possible.
A prince of Egypt!

189
00:15:59.327 --> 00:16:04.327
He is not a prince of Egypt.
He is not the son of your sister.

190
00:16:05.407 --> 00:16:08.167
He is the son of Hebrew slaves.

191
00:16:12.927 --> 00:16:14.727
Speak...

192
00:16:14.767 --> 00:16:16.967
my son.

193
00:16:20.927 --> 00:16:25.927
I am the son of Amram and Yochabel.
Hebrew slaves.

194
00:16:33.927 --> 00:16:38.687
My brother. it was I
who deceived you. not Moses.

195
00:16:38.767 --> 00:16:41.887
- He was only a child.
- Leave me.

196
00:16:41.967 --> 00:16:45.167
I shall not see your face again.

197
00:16:58.847 --> 00:17:00.407
Come to me.

198
00:17:07.927 --> 00:17:12.527
I do not care who you are
or what you are.

199
00:17:12.607 --> 00:17:14.647
but...

200
00:17:14.687 --> 00:17:19.927
I want to hear from your own lips
that you are not a traitor.

201
00:17:19.967 --> 00:17:24.967
that you would not lead these people
in revolt against me.

202
00:17:26.007 --> 00:17:28.727
Tell me. Moses. I will believe you.

203
00:17:31.927 --> 00:17:34.567
I am not this deliverer you fear.

204
00:17:34.607 --> 00:17:39.927
It would take more than a man
to lead the slaves from bondage.

205
00:17:39.967 --> 00:17:42.567
It would take a god.

206
00:17:43.567 --> 00:17:46.247
But if I COULD free them.

207
00:17:46.287 --> 00:17:48.927
I would.

208
00:17:50.927 --> 00:17:53.647
What has turned you against me?

209
00:17:54.687 --> 00:17:57.967
From the time my sister brought you
to the court. I loved you.

210
00:17:58.047 --> 00:18:01.487
reared you.
set you before my own son.

211
00:18:01.567 --> 00:18:04.167
because I saw in you...

212
00:18:04.207 --> 00:18:08.727
a worth and a greatness
above other men.

213
00:18:08.807 --> 00:18:11.847
No son could have
more love for you than I.

214
00:18:12.847 --> 00:18:16.447
Then why are you forcing me
to destroy you?

215
00:18:16.527 --> 00:18:19.327
What evil has done THIS to you?

216
00:18:19.367 --> 00:18:25.927
The evil that men should turn their
brothers into beasts of burden.

217
00:18:25.967 --> 00:18:30.007
to slave and suffer in dumb anguish.

218
00:18:30.047 --> 00:18:35.047
to be stripped of spirit
and hope and faith.

219
00:18:35.127 --> 00:18:40.127
only because they're
of another race. another creed.

220
00:18:40.207 --> 00:18:45.207
If there IS a God.
he did not mean this to be so.

221
00:18:49.927 --> 00:18:54.767
What I have done.
I was compelled to do.

222
00:18:59.127 --> 00:19:01.167
So be it.

223
00:19:01.247 --> 00:19:04.127
What I do now...

224
00:19:04.167 --> 00:19:07.207
I am compelled to do.

225
00:19:08.247 --> 00:19:11.527
No! No!

226
00:19:16.927 --> 00:19:18.807
Rameses...

227
00:19:18.847 --> 00:19:21.647
Egypt shall be yours.

228
00:19:27.247 --> 00:19:29.607
Hear what I say. Rameses.

229
00:19:30.927 --> 00:19:35.927
When I cross the river of death.
you will be Pharaoh in Egypt.

230
00:19:37.967 --> 00:19:40.567
Harden yourself against subordinates.

231
00:19:41.927 --> 00:19:44.647
Put no faith in a brother.

232
00:19:44.687 --> 00:19:47.327
Have no friend.

233
00:19:48.407 --> 00:19:51.087
Trust no woman.

234
00:19:55.927 --> 00:19:58.567
I protected the helpless.

235
00:19:58.607 --> 00:20:01.327
I nourished the orphan.

236
00:20:01.367 --> 00:20:03.727
Great one!

237
00:20:06.407 --> 00:20:11.007
He who ate my bread
and called me Father...

238
00:20:11.047 --> 00:20:13.927
would make rebellion against me.

239
00:20:14.967 --> 00:20:18.647
What manner of death
do you decree for him?

240
00:20:22.927 --> 00:20:25.567
I cannot speak it.

241
00:20:25.607 --> 00:20:28.207
Let it be as you will.

242
00:20:30.327 --> 00:20:33.167
I will not live if you must die!

243
00:20:37.567 --> 00:20:41.647
The feet of a Hebrew slave
is not the right place

244
00:20:41.687 --> 00:20:43.887
for the next queen of Egypt.

245
00:20:48.367 --> 00:20:50.567
Take him away.

246
00:20:56.887 --> 00:20:59.487
Do not look upon the traitor.

247
00:21:06.367 --> 00:21:13.287
Let the name of Moses be stricken
from every book and tablet.

248
00:21:16.367 --> 00:21:20.887
Stricken from all pylons
and obelisks.

249
00:21:20.967 --> 00:21:25.087
Stricken from
every monument of Egypt.

250
00:21:28.247 --> 00:21:33.407
Let the name of...Moses...

251
00:21:33.447 --> 00:21:36.247
be unheard and unspoken...

252
00:21:37.927 --> 00:21:40.447
erased from the memory of men...

253
00:21:42.327 --> 00:21:44.287
for all time.

254
00:21:59.927 --> 00:22:02.367
No. Moses.

255
00:22:02.447 --> 00:22:06.047
It is I who will possess all of her.

256
00:22:06.087 --> 00:22:11.847
You think when you are in my arms
it will be HIS face you will see?

257
00:22:11.927 --> 00:22:14.567
Yes. Only his face.

258
00:22:14.607 --> 00:22:19.447
I defeated you in life. You shall
not defeat me by your death.

259
00:22:19.527 --> 00:22:24.047
The dead are not scorched
in the desert of desire.

260
00:22:24.087 --> 00:22:27.687
They do not suffer
from the thirst of passion

261
00:22:27.727 --> 00:22:32.927
or stagger towards
some mirage of lost love.

262
00:22:32.967 --> 00:22:36.407
But you. Hebrew.
will suffer all these things...

263
00:22:36.447 --> 00:22:40.207
- by living.
- You will let him live!

264
00:22:40.247 --> 00:22:42.887
I will not make him a martyr.

265
00:22:42.927 --> 00:22:46.887
No phantom will come between us
in the night.

266
00:22:47.887 --> 00:22:52.167
Yes. my sweet. I will let him live.

267
00:22:52.207 --> 00:22:53.927
Dead...

268
00:22:53.967 --> 00:22:56.567
you alone would possess him.

269
00:22:57.607 --> 00:23:00.887
From where I send him
there is no returning.

270
00:23:01.927 --> 00:23:04.567
And you will never know

271
00:23:04.607 --> 00:23:09.607
if he has found forgetfulness
within another woman's arms.

272
00:23:13.927 --> 00:23:17.927
Now. look upon each other
for the last time.

273
00:23:53.087 --> 00:23:57.527
Now look for the first time.
Abiram. upon the governor of Goshen.

274
00:23:59.247 --> 00:24:03.367
Dathan. my brother.
you have the favour of the Lord.

275
00:24:03.447 --> 00:24:06.247
I prefer the gratitude
of the prince.

276
00:24:22.927 --> 00:24:24.407
Nearer.

277
00:24:27.927 --> 00:24:30.487
Yes. Very lovely.

278
00:24:31.527 --> 00:24:33.487
Not that purplish flower.

279
00:24:34.927 --> 00:24:37.567
The purity of white...

280
00:24:37.607 --> 00:24:40.247
will cool the blush of your cheek.

281
00:24:43.927 --> 00:24:47.927
Leave us. All of you.
You. too. my brother.

282
00:24:47.967 --> 00:24:52.327
Continue your playing...
but in the house.

283
00:24:54.927 --> 00:24:57.727
Yes. That's better.

284
00:25:01.127 --> 00:25:03.927
A flower behind a flower.

285
00:25:04.927 --> 00:25:08.367
Dathan. if you fear God. let me go.

286
00:25:08.447 --> 00:25:11.407
I'm here. girl.
because I put no trust

287
00:25:11.447 --> 00:25:14.807
in a desert god
and his mud-pit prophet.

288
00:25:14.847 --> 00:25:18.207
I prospered because I bowed low
before the Egyptians.

289
00:25:18.287 --> 00:25:21.727
Now the Egyptians bow low before me.

290
00:25:22.727 --> 00:25:24.687
Joshua wanted you.

291
00:25:27.287 --> 00:25:29.567
Baka wanted you.

292
00:25:29.607 --> 00:25:32.247
But you belong to ME.

293
00:25:32.287 --> 00:25:35.887
A gift from Rameses
to His Excellency.

294
00:25:40.927 --> 00:25:43.727
I will bow before you. Dathan.

295
00:25:44.727 --> 00:25:47.407
I will work my hands raw for you.

296
00:25:48.647 --> 00:25:50.927
But please...

297
00:25:50.967 --> 00:25:55.007
please do not shame me
before my Lord.

298
00:25:55.047 --> 00:25:57.647
Your Lord is the governor of Goshen.

299
00:25:57.687 --> 00:26:00.407
What difference to my shame?

300
00:26:00.447 --> 00:26:04.207
No difference to you.

301
00:26:04.247 --> 00:26:07.127
But to a condemned slave
like Joshua...

302
00:26:08.367 --> 00:26:12.727
it could make the difference
between death on the spikes

303
00:26:12.767 --> 00:26:16.047
and life in
the copper mines of Sinai.

304
00:26:18.087 --> 00:26:22.207
What would you do to influence
His Excellency's clemency?

305
00:26:25.927 --> 00:26:28.367
Anything. Dathan.

306
00:26:29.927 --> 00:26:31.887
Anything.

307
00:26:32.967 --> 00:26:35.807
Joshua will always
be grateful to you...

308
00:26:37.927 --> 00:26:40.487
my little mud flower.

309
00:26:41.927 --> 00:26:46.127
His fate is better
than the one that waits for Moses.

310
00:26:57.927 --> 00:27:00.567
The slave who would be king.

311
00:27:01.487 --> 00:27:04.447
Captain. Robe of state.

312
00:27:05.127 --> 00:27:09.487
His Hebrew mother brought it
to the prison before she died.

313
00:27:14.567 --> 00:27:17.447
I'd rather this for your armour.

314
00:27:17.487 --> 00:27:20.167
You will have need of a sceptre.

315
00:27:20.207 --> 00:27:22.927
Give me this binding pole.

316
00:27:27.927 --> 00:27:30.567
Here is your king's sceptre

317
00:27:30.607 --> 00:27:33.247
and here is your kingdom...

318
00:27:34.247 --> 00:27:39.327
with the scorpion. the cobra
and the lizard for subjects.

319
00:27:39.367 --> 00:27:44.447
Free THEM. if you will.
Leave the Hebrews to me.

320
00:27:44.487 --> 00:27:49.247
Give this prince of Israel
one day's ration of bread and water.

321
00:27:49.327 --> 00:27:54.527
It will take many days to cross this
wilderness. if he can cross at all.

322
00:28:00.127 --> 00:28:05.367
I commend you to your Hebrew god
who has no name.

323
00:28:05.407 --> 00:28:10.007
If you die. it will be
by his hand. not by mine.

324
00:28:39.527 --> 00:28:42.727
Farewell. my one-time brother.

325
00:28:55.927 --> 00:28:59.287
Into the blistering wilderness.

326
00:28:59.327 --> 00:29:03.407
the man who walked
with kings now walks alone.

327
00:29:04.407 --> 00:29:07.607
Torn from the pinnacle
of royal power.

328
00:29:07.687 --> 00:29:10.887
stripped of all rank
and earthly wealth.

329
00:29:10.967 --> 00:29:16.047
a forsaken man
without a country. without a hope.

330
00:29:16.087 --> 00:29:21.607
His soul in turmoil.
like the hot winds and raging sands

331
00:29:21.647 --> 00:29:26.767
that lash him with the fury
of a taskmaster's whip.

332
00:29:26.807 --> 00:29:30.767
He is driven forward. always forward

333
00:29:30.807 --> 00:29:33.167
by a god unknown

334
00:29:33.247 --> 00:29:36.007
toward a land unseen.

335
00:29:38.087 --> 00:29:41.127
Into the molten wilderness of sin.

336
00:29:41.207 --> 00:29:45.287
where granite sentinels
stand as towers of living death

337
00:29:45.327 --> 00:29:47.367
to bar his way.

338
00:29:47.407 --> 00:29:52.607
Each night brings the black
embrace of loneliness.

339
00:29:52.647 --> 00:29:55.327
In the mocking whisper of the wind

340
00:29:55.367 --> 00:29:58.567
he hears the echoing voices
of the dark.

341
00:30:13.447 --> 00:30:19.367
His tortured mind wondering if they
call the memory of past triumphs

342
00:30:19.447 --> 00:30:23.887
or wail foreboding
of disasters yet to come...

343
00:30:23.927 --> 00:30:29.927
or whether the desert's hot breath
has melted his reason into madness.

344
00:30:31.847 --> 00:30:36.967
He cannot cool the burning kiss
of thirst upon his lips.

345
00:30:37.007 --> 00:30:39.967
nor shade the scorching fury
of the sun.

346
00:30:41.927 --> 00:30:44.647
All about is desolation.

347
00:30:46.007 --> 00:30:51.247
He can neither bless nor curse
the power that moves him.

348
00:30:51.287 --> 00:30:55.247
for he does not know
from where it comes.

349
00:30:58.247 --> 00:31:01.927
Learning that it can be more
terrible to live than to die.

350
00:31:01.967 --> 00:31:06.967
he is driven onward through
the burning crucible of desert.

351
00:31:07.047 --> 00:31:11.807
where holy men and prophets
are cleansed and purged

352
00:31:11.887 --> 00:31:15.727
for God's great purpose.

353
00:31:15.767 --> 00:31:20.607
Until. at last.
at the end of human strength.

354
00:31:20.647 --> 00:31:24.327
beaten into the dust
from which he came.

355
00:31:24.407 --> 00:31:27.687
the metal is ready
for the Maker's hand.

356
00:31:46.687 --> 00:31:52.367
And he found strength
from a fruit-laden palm tree

357
00:31:52.447 --> 00:31:57.207
and life-giving water.
flowing from the well of Midian.

358
00:32:09.647 --> 00:32:12.687
- If only sheep were men!
- Unmarried men!

359
00:32:12.767 --> 00:32:17.527
- Can you think of nothing else?
- I don't know. I've never tried!

360
00:32:17.607 --> 00:32:21.487
You needn't have painted your nails.
There isn't a man from here to Horeb.

361
00:32:33.247 --> 00:32:37.167
- What do you see. Sephora?
- What are you looking at?

362
00:32:37.207 --> 00:32:39.647
- A man.
- What?

363
00:32:43.327 --> 00:32:46.367
- Only one?
- Is he handsome?

364
00:32:46.407 --> 00:32:48.287
- Look at his sandals!
- Egyptian!

365
00:32:48.367 --> 00:32:51.407
- His robe is not Egyptian.
- Who cares?

366
00:32:53.767 --> 00:32:57.447
- He's eaten a whole bunch of dates!
- Could it be dangerous?

367
00:32:57.487 --> 00:33:00.327
- Are you sure he's alive?
- I hope so!

368
00:33:00.367 --> 00:33:02.487
Look. There's REAL trouble.

369
00:33:07.887 --> 00:33:09.847
Amalekites.

370
00:33:13.887 --> 00:33:18.407
- I'll talk to them.
- Talk? Get stones!

371
00:33:22.767 --> 00:33:26.887
- We drew this water!
- Out of the way. girl!

372
00:33:26.967 --> 00:33:30.727
This is the well of Jethro.
our father. You have no right here!

373
00:33:30.807 --> 00:33:33.007
Our goats don't know your father!

374
00:33:33.047 --> 00:33:36.247
- Jethro's mark is on the well.
- They can't read!

375
00:33:36.327 --> 00:33:38.207
Nor can we!

376
00:33:38.287 --> 00:33:42.647
- He's the Sheik of Midian!
- Then let him breed sons!

377
00:33:58.007 --> 00:34:00.767
Let them be first
whose hands have drawn the water.

378
00:34:00.807 --> 00:34:04.927
The stranger is wise...and strong.

379
00:34:05.007 --> 00:34:08.607
Drive back your goats
until the sheep are watered.

380
00:34:24.847 --> 00:34:29.447
We should draw water for YOU
and wash the dust from your feet.

381
00:34:33.367 --> 00:34:36.487
Let me first remove his sandals!

382
00:34:36.567 --> 00:34:40.007
Never did a lost sheep
have so many shepherds.

383
00:34:40.087 --> 00:34:42.927
- We have no towel.
- My veil will serve.

384
00:34:42.967 --> 00:34:46.167
Let me pour the water!

385
00:34:46.247 --> 00:34:49.847
- Am I to be bathed or drowned?
- I'll hold it!

386
00:34:49.887 --> 00:34:53.407
Is it true that Egyptian girls
paint their eyes?

387
00:34:53.447 --> 00:34:57.447
Yes. But very few have eyes
as beautiful as yours.

388
00:34:59.607 --> 00:35:04.927
And who...? Who is the brave one
who stood against the Amalekites?

389
00:35:04.967 --> 00:35:07.247
That's Sephora. She's the oldest.

390
00:35:08.727 --> 00:35:12.767
Since you have already
divided the stranger among you.

391
00:35:12.807 --> 00:35:15.367
I will ask a welcome for him.

392
00:35:15.407 --> 00:35:18.847
- Our father is Jethro.
- He's Sheik of Midian.

393
00:35:43.007 --> 00:35:44.807
Strength to you. stranger.

394
00:35:44.887 --> 00:35:48.927
I am Moses.
Son of Amram and Yochabel.

395
00:35:48.967 --> 00:35:53.247
Health. prosperity. life to you.
Jethro of Midian.

396
00:35:58.047 --> 00:36:01.007
Sephora has told me
of your kindness.

397
00:36:01.047 --> 00:36:03.847
Let us break bread
while she brings meat.

398
00:36:07.247 --> 00:36:09.287
You have come far.

399
00:36:10.527 --> 00:36:15.527
- From Egypt.
- Across the desert? On foot?

400
00:36:15.607 --> 00:36:19.207
He who has no name
surely guided your steps.

401
00:36:20.207 --> 00:36:24.647
No name? You Bedouins
know the god of Abraham?

402
00:36:24.727 --> 00:36:27.567
Abraham is the father
of many nations.

403
00:36:27.607 --> 00:36:30.887
We are the children of lshmael.
his first-born.

404
00:36:30.967 --> 00:36:34.407
We are the obedient of God.

405
00:36:34.447 --> 00:36:37.207
My people look to him
for deliverance.

406
00:36:39.487 --> 00:36:41.847
But they are still in bondage.

407
00:36:44.607 --> 00:36:48.367
Tomorrow we go to the high pastures
beneath God's holy mountain.

408
00:36:48.447 --> 00:36:51.247
My tent would be favoured
if you joined us.

409
00:36:54.007 --> 00:36:56.567
I am a stranger in a strange land.

410
00:36:56.607 --> 00:37:00.047
I have no wealth.
no skill as a shepherd.

411
00:37:01.167 --> 00:37:05.927
And it is...death to give
sanctuary to a runaway slave.

412
00:37:05.967 --> 00:37:07.927
Slave?

413
00:37:07.967 --> 00:37:12.967
Not among our people. You have
wisdom. You need nothing more.

414
00:37:13.007 --> 00:37:16.767
And there are seven to teach you
the tasks of a shepherd.

415
00:37:18.247 --> 00:37:22.847
- Sephora is the eldest.
- You can learn best from her.

416
00:37:27.687 --> 00:37:29.727
I will dwell in this land.

417
00:37:49.807 --> 00:37:53.167
- Today he sleeps.
- Who sleeps?

418
00:37:54.327 --> 00:37:56.607
He who has no name.

419
00:37:57.967 --> 00:38:01.007
Did God live on this mountain?

420
00:38:01.087 --> 00:38:04.047
Sinai is his high place. His temple.

421
00:38:06.047 --> 00:38:08.167
If this god IS God.

422
00:38:08.207 --> 00:38:12.047
he would live on every mountain.
in every valley.

423
00:38:13.327 --> 00:38:17.927
He would not be only the god
of Israel or of lshmael alone.

424
00:38:17.967 --> 00:38:20.567
but of ALL men.

425
00:38:20.607 --> 00:38:24.207
It is said he created all men
in his image.

426
00:38:24.287 --> 00:38:29.287
And he would dwell in every heart.
in every mind...

427
00:38:29.327 --> 00:38:31.367
in every soul.

428
00:38:35.527 --> 00:38:39.367
I do not know about such things.

429
00:38:39.407 --> 00:38:43.847
But I DO know that the mountain
rumbles when God is there.

430
00:38:43.927 --> 00:38:49.527
And the earth trembles
and the cloud is red with fire.

431
00:38:49.567 --> 00:38:54.567
At such a time. has any man ever
gone to see him face to face?

432
00:38:54.647 --> 00:38:59.407
No man has ever set foot
on the forbidden slopes of Sinai.

433
00:39:00.727 --> 00:39:03.087
Why do you want to see him. Moses?

434
00:39:03.167 --> 00:39:06.207
To know that he is.

435
00:39:06.287 --> 00:39:11.127
And if he is. to know why
he has not heard the cries of slaves.

436
00:39:11.167 --> 00:39:15.367
Moses. it would be death
to look upon his face.

437
00:39:16.447 --> 00:39:20.967
How many of my people have died
because he turned away his face?

438
00:39:22.047 --> 00:39:24.887
Can a man judge God?

439
00:39:24.927 --> 00:39:30.687
No. Moses.
We cannot see his whole purpose.

440
00:39:30.727 --> 00:39:35.007
Even lshmael did not know that God
drove him into the desert

441
00:39:35.047 --> 00:39:38.087
to be the father of a nation.

442
00:39:38.167 --> 00:39:42.927
Is it not enough to know that he has
saved you from the Pharaoh's anger?

443
00:39:44.767 --> 00:39:47.207
How do you know that?

444
00:39:48.247 --> 00:39:52.847
You walk like a prince.
And you fight like a warrior.

445
00:39:52.887 --> 00:39:55.767
There is word in the caravans
of a great one

446
00:39:55.807 --> 00:39:58.487
who was driven out of Egypt.

447
00:40:00.567 --> 00:40:03.607
This is not the sceptre
of a prince...

448
00:40:03.647 --> 00:40:06.007
but the staff of a wanderer.

449
00:40:07.247 --> 00:40:10.687
Then rest from wandering.

450
00:40:10.727 --> 00:40:12.927
My father has many flocks

451
00:40:13.007 --> 00:40:15.887
and no son to tend them.

452
00:40:15.927 --> 00:40:19.607
There would be peace of spirit
for you. Moses.

453
00:40:19.647 --> 00:40:24.647
in our tents
beneath the holy mountain.

454
00:40:24.727 --> 00:40:27.767
You have strong faith in this God.

455
00:40:30.007 --> 00:40:32.647
But. for me.
there is no peace of spirit

456
00:40:32.687 --> 00:40:36.207
until I hear the word of God...

457
00:40:36.287 --> 00:40:38.487
from God himself.

458
00:40:50.847 --> 00:40:53.807
I wish every day
was a shearing festival!

459
00:40:53.887 --> 00:40:57.087
And all the men following you
like sheep to be sheared!

460
00:40:57.167 --> 00:41:00.767
- One would be enough!
- If he were Moses!

461
00:41:02.207 --> 00:41:06.247
Never before has our wool
brought so rich a payment.

462
00:41:06.287 --> 00:41:11.047
Moses has sold the whole shearing
of all the tribes in one piece.

463
00:41:11.087 --> 00:41:14.687
His words are truth.
His trading is just.

464
00:41:14.727 --> 00:41:17.927
Peace be with you. sheiks of Sinai.

465
00:41:18.007 --> 00:41:20.207
Why are you dressed like that?

466
00:41:20.287 --> 00:41:23.247
Aren't you dancing with us
before the sheiks?

467
00:41:23.327 --> 00:41:27.847
No. I am not going to dance
before the sheiks. Here.

468
00:41:27.887 --> 00:41:32.647
And I am not going to be displayed
like a caravan's wares

469
00:41:32.687 --> 00:41:35.407
before Moses or any other man.

470
00:41:36.487 --> 00:41:39.447
Tonight I tend the sheep.

471
00:41:39.527 --> 00:41:43.607
You needn't laugh.
Moses may not choose YOU either!

472
00:41:46.167 --> 00:41:49.127
Moses shall no longer
be a stranger among us.

473
00:41:49.207 --> 00:41:51.647
- Give him of our flocks.
- And let him choose.

474
00:41:51.687 --> 00:41:57.367
I shall give him choice
of my seven daughters for wife.

475
00:41:58.567 --> 00:42:01.847
The shadow of my wisdom has fled.

476
00:42:01.927 --> 00:42:05.047
Can a man choose
from among the stars of the sky?

477
00:42:05.127 --> 00:42:09.647
Consider them as they dance.
Cohab. strike a bow.

478
00:42:30.367 --> 00:42:33.487
- A pleasant task.
- Indeed!

479
00:42:36.327 --> 00:42:40.287
A bride. a shawl.
Choose one. not all.

480
00:42:40.327 --> 00:42:44.407
One shawl. one wife.
Your choice for life.

481
00:42:55.887 --> 00:42:58.687
One is a great price.

482
00:43:16.847 --> 00:43:19.287
- Which. Moses?
- Which will it be?

483
00:43:19.327 --> 00:43:21.207
Make your choice. Moses.

484
00:43:21.287 --> 00:43:24.047
It is a garden of many flowers.

485
00:43:24.087 --> 00:43:28.167
I wish you had my years
and I had your choice.

486
00:43:29.247 --> 00:43:34.607
In the tent of Jethro
there is dignity. honour. freedom...

487
00:43:34.647 --> 00:43:36.527
and beauty.

488
00:43:36.567 --> 00:43:39.367
All that a man could ask of life.

489
00:43:39.407 --> 00:43:42.687
But my heart is still
a prisoner of the past.

490
00:43:42.727 --> 00:43:45.687
I...I cannot choose now.

491
00:43:47.767 --> 00:43:51.207
- Strength to you. sheiks of Sinai.
- May God guide your heart.

492
00:43:53.287 --> 00:43:54.687
Moses...!

493
00:44:03.527 --> 00:44:05.327
Tonight he is awake.

494
00:44:08.847 --> 00:44:11.727
Which of my sisters did you choose?

495
00:44:14.767 --> 00:44:17.487
I made no choice. Sephora.

496
00:44:23.047 --> 00:44:25.927
She was very beautiful. wasn't she?

497
00:44:25.967 --> 00:44:30.647
This woman of Egypt
who left her scar upon your heart.

498
00:44:35.167 --> 00:44:39.127
Whose skin was white as curd.

499
00:44:39.167 --> 00:44:42.927
Her eyes.
green as the cedars of Lebanon.

500
00:44:42.967 --> 00:44:46.247
Her lips. tamarisk honey.

501
00:44:46.327 --> 00:44:49.927
Like the breast of a dove.
her arms were soft.

502
00:44:52.047 --> 00:44:55.167
And the wine of desire
was in her veins.

503
00:44:56.367 --> 00:44:59.247
Yes. She was beautiful...

504
00:45:00.887 --> 00:45:03.087
as a jewel.

505
00:45:03.687 --> 00:45:08.287
A jewel has brilliant fire...
but gives no warmth.

506
00:45:12.127 --> 00:45:16.647
Our hands are not so soft
but they can serve.

507
00:45:16.687 --> 00:45:21.607
Our bodies not so white.
but they are strong.

508
00:45:21.647 --> 00:45:24.847
Our lips are not perfumed...

509
00:45:25.927 --> 00:45:28.367
but they speak the truth.

510
00:45:29.807 --> 00:45:32.687
Love is not an art to us.

511
00:45:32.727 --> 00:45:35.327
It's life to us.

512
00:45:37.367 --> 00:45:40.967
We are not dressed
in gold and fine linen.

513
00:45:42.167 --> 00:45:45.127
Strength and honour are our clothing.

514
00:45:46.287 --> 00:45:50.807
Our tents are not
the columned halls of Egypt...

515
00:45:50.847 --> 00:45:54.367
but our children
play happily before them.

516
00:45:56.607 --> 00:45:59.327
We can offer you little...

517
00:46:01.407 --> 00:46:04.367
but we offer all we have.

518
00:46:04.447 --> 00:46:08.887
I have not little. Sephora.
I have nothing.

519
00:46:08.967 --> 00:46:13.887
Nothing from some
is more than gold from others.

520
00:46:16.087 --> 00:46:19.527
You would fill
the emptiness of my heart.

521
00:46:22.847 --> 00:46:26.687
I could never fill all of it. Moses.

522
00:46:26.727 --> 00:46:30.007
But I shall not
be jealous of a memory.

523
00:47:12.287 --> 00:47:15.327
May the gods bless you

524
00:47:15.367 --> 00:47:20.687
as you go to join them
in the land of the dead.

525
00:47:22.247 --> 00:47:24.847
The old windbag.

526
00:47:26.207 --> 00:47:29.047
What an infernal fuss.

527
00:47:30.127 --> 00:47:33.727
After all.
dying is only a part of living.

528
00:47:33.807 --> 00:47:36.607
You won't die. old crocodile.

529
00:47:36.647 --> 00:47:41.327
You'll cheat death the way
you cheat me at hounds and jackals.

530
00:47:41.367 --> 00:47:45.407
I'm afraid he won't let me cheat
the way you do.

531
00:47:48.927 --> 00:47:52.127
You'll be Pharaoh by sunset. Rameses.

532
00:47:54.247 --> 00:47:58.327
I hope you're content...at last.

533
00:47:59.367 --> 00:48:03.047
I am content to be your son.

534
00:48:03.127 --> 00:48:06.567
You have restored Egypt
to her greatness.

535
00:48:06.607 --> 00:48:10.567
I shall make her greatness
feared among nations.

536
00:48:10.607 --> 00:48:14.527
No doubt. no doubt.
You can overcome anything...

537
00:48:14.567 --> 00:48:17.607
but your own arrogance.

538
00:48:17.687 --> 00:48:20.727
Don't exhaust yourself. great one.

539
00:48:20.767 --> 00:48:23.207
Dear great one.

540
00:48:23.287 --> 00:48:25.727
Why not. kitten?

541
00:48:25.807 --> 00:48:30.087
You are the only thing
I regret leaving.

542
00:48:30.167 --> 00:48:32.927
You have been my joy.

543
00:48:32.967 --> 00:48:35.087
And you. my only love.

544
00:48:35.167 --> 00:48:36.887
Uh-huh.

545
00:48:38.447 --> 00:48:41.967
Now YOU'RE cheating.

546
00:48:42.047 --> 00:48:45.807
- There was another.
- Yes.

547
00:48:48.047 --> 00:48:50.087
I know.

548
00:48:52.007 --> 00:48:55.287
I loved him. too.

549
00:48:55.367 --> 00:48:58.967
With my last breath.
I'll break my own law

550
00:48:59.047 --> 00:49:01.607
and speak the name of...

551
00:49:03.767 --> 00:49:05.887
Moses.

552
00:49:19.767 --> 00:49:24.527
The royal falcon
has flown into the sun.

553
00:49:47.487 --> 00:49:50.687
Did the little boy die in the desert.
my father?

554
00:49:50.767 --> 00:49:55.207
No. God brought lshmael and
his mother. Hagar. to a good land.

555
00:49:55.247 --> 00:49:58.207
The same God who lives
on the mountain?

556
00:49:58.287 --> 00:50:00.727
It may be. my son.

557
00:50:03.767 --> 00:50:06.327
Your mother is calling.

558
00:50:08.367 --> 00:50:09.407
Here!

559
00:50:11.887 --> 00:50:16.007
Moses!
There is a man among the sheep!

560
00:50:16.087 --> 00:50:17.727
You stay...

561
00:50:19.767 --> 00:50:23.887
Keep sounding the alarm.
Stay here till your mother comes.

562
00:50:28.847 --> 00:50:31.127
In the cleft. behind the rock.

563
00:50:31.167 --> 00:50:34.207
Your eyes are sharp
as well as beautiful.

564
00:50:49.287 --> 00:50:51.567
Tokar!

565
00:50:51.647 --> 00:50:54.367
Setaft! Back!

566
00:50:54.407 --> 00:50:56.767
Setaft. back!

567
00:51:00.287 --> 00:51:02.727
Come down!

568
00:51:06.807 --> 00:51:09.167
Down. Tokar!

569
00:51:12.207 --> 00:51:16.127
Praise God I have found you!

570
00:51:16.167 --> 00:51:18.207
Joshua?

571
00:51:18.247 --> 00:51:20.207
We thought you dead.

572
00:51:20.287 --> 00:51:24.327
In the copper mines.
the living ARE dead.

573
00:51:24.367 --> 00:51:27.327
Sephora! Bring water.

574
00:51:32.607 --> 00:51:34.567
How did you find me?

575
00:51:34.607 --> 00:51:38.967
A merchant buying copper
saw you in the tent of Jethro.

576
00:51:41.887 --> 00:51:44.767
Here. you too will find peace.

577
00:51:45.847 --> 00:51:47.887
Peace?

578
00:51:47.967 --> 00:51:50.927
How can you find peace or want it.

579
00:51:50.967 --> 00:51:55.047
when Rameses builds cities mortared
with the blood of our people?

580
00:51:55.087 --> 00:51:57.727
You must lead them out of Egypt!

581
00:51:57.767 --> 00:52:02.287
God made a covenant with Abraham
that HE would deliver the people.

582
00:52:02.367 --> 00:52:05.127
Am I the hand of God?

583
00:52:05.167 --> 00:52:09.167
- Sephora. give him water.
- Water! Bless you!

584
00:52:09.207 --> 00:52:12.567
The desert sun
has set fire to his mind.

585
00:52:12.647 --> 00:52:15.007
His name is Joshua.

586
00:52:15.087 --> 00:52:19.087
I once killed that he might live.

587
00:52:19.127 --> 00:52:23.167
They said you were condemned
but I knew you were chosen

588
00:52:23.207 --> 00:52:26.047
to take the sword of God
into your hand!

589
00:52:26.087 --> 00:52:27.367
I am not the man.

590
00:52:29.847 --> 00:52:32.287
I am a shepherd with flocks...

591
00:52:33.767 --> 00:52:36.527
That light on the mountainside...

592
00:52:37.967 --> 00:52:41.007
Do you see that strange fire?

593
00:52:41.087 --> 00:52:43.847
- A bush that burns?
- No.

594
00:52:43.887 --> 00:52:46.327
It is on fire
but the bush does not burn.

595
00:52:46.407 --> 00:52:51.167
Sephora. take him.
Serve him food in our tent.

596
00:52:51.207 --> 00:52:54.567
I will turn aside
and see this great sight.

597
00:54:26.847 --> 00:54:29.207
I am here.

598
00:54:29.247 --> 00:54:33.087
Put off thy shoes from off thy feet.

599
00:54:33.127 --> 00:54:38.647
For the place whereon thou standest
is holy ground.

600
00:54:43.567 --> 00:54:47.167
I am the God of thy father.

601
00:54:49.047 --> 00:54:51.567
The God of Abraham.

602
00:54:51.607 --> 00:54:55.567
the God of lsaac
and the God of Jacob.

603
00:54:57.687 --> 00:55:00.047
Lord...

604
00:55:01.127 --> 00:55:04.327
Lord. why do you not hear the cries

605
00:55:04.367 --> 00:55:07.567
of their children
in the bondage of Egypt?

606
00:55:07.607 --> 00:55:12.607
I have surely seen the affliction
of my people which are in Egypt.

607
00:55:14.127 --> 00:55:20.287
And I have heard their cry
by reason of their taskmasters.

608
00:55:20.327 --> 00:55:22.767
For I know their sorrows.

609
00:55:23.967 --> 00:55:29.647
Therefore. I will send thee.
Moses. unto Pharaoh.

610
00:55:29.687 --> 00:55:34.207
that thou mayest bring my people
out of Egypt.

611
00:55:34.247 --> 00:55:38.687
Who am l. Lord.
that you should send me?

612
00:55:40.807 --> 00:55:44.327
How can I lead this people
out of bondage?

613
00:55:45.327 --> 00:55:49.287
What words can I speak
that they will heed?

614
00:55:49.327 --> 00:55:53.607
I will teach thee what thou wilt say.

615
00:55:53.647 --> 00:55:57.487
When thou hast brought forth
the people.

616
00:55:57.527 --> 00:56:02.447
they shall serve me
upon this mountain.

617
00:56:02.527 --> 00:56:06.127
I will put my laws into their hearts.

618
00:56:06.167 --> 00:56:11.087
And in their minds will I write them.

619
00:56:11.127 --> 00:56:14.567
Now. therefore. go.

620
00:56:14.647 --> 00:56:17.087
And I will be with thee.

621
00:56:17.167 --> 00:56:19.847
But if I say to your children

622
00:56:19.887 --> 00:56:23.327
that the God of their fathers
has sent me.

623
00:56:23.407 --> 00:56:26.287
they will ask. "What is his name?"

624
00:56:26.367 --> 00:56:28.967
And how shall I answer them?

625
00:56:30.287 --> 00:56:33.487
I am that I am.

626
00:56:35.007 --> 00:56:40.687
Thou shalt say.
"I AM hath sent me on to you.

627
00:56:53.327 --> 00:56:55.927
Is the holy mountain
forbidden to men?

628
00:56:55.967 --> 00:56:59.327
Yes. And I am afraid for him.

629
00:56:59.407 --> 00:57:02.927
Then he is more than man. for look...

630
00:57:17.327 --> 00:57:19.887
Look at his face.

631
00:57:19.927 --> 00:57:22.687
He has seen God.

632
00:57:39.807 --> 00:57:45.247
Moses...your hair...your sandals.

633
00:57:45.327 --> 00:57:49.407
I stood upon holy ground.

634
00:57:49.447 --> 00:57:52.087
Can you tell us. Moses?

635
00:57:52.127 --> 00:57:54.567
My eyes could not look upon him.

636
00:57:54.647 --> 00:57:57.167
Did he speak?

637
00:57:57.207 --> 00:58:00.087
He revealed his word to my mind.

638
00:58:01.967 --> 00:58:04.087
And the word was God.

639
00:58:04.167 --> 00:58:07.047
Did he speak as a man?

640
00:58:07.127 --> 00:58:10.007
He is not flesh but spirit.

641
00:58:10.087 --> 00:58:13.287
The light of eternal mind.

642
00:58:13.367 --> 00:58:16.567
And I know that his light
is in every man.

643
00:58:16.647 --> 00:58:19.447
Did he ask something of you?

644
00:58:21.727 --> 00:58:24.687
That I go to Egypt.

645
00:58:24.727 --> 00:58:29.087
You ARE God's messenger!
He has set the day of deliverance.

646
00:58:29.127 --> 00:58:32.247
I will get water and bread
that we may leave at once.

647
00:58:32.327 --> 00:58:35.047
But Egypt holds death for you.

648
00:58:35.087 --> 00:58:38.127
If it be his will.

649
00:58:38.167 --> 00:58:40.967
Where he sends you. I shall go.

650
00:58:41.007 --> 00:58:43.447
Your God is my God.

651
00:58:43.527 --> 00:58:47.727
I will lead men against the armoury
and get swords!

652
00:58:47.807 --> 00:58:52.007
It is not by the sword
that he will deliver his people.

653
00:58:52.087 --> 00:58:54.527
but by the staff of a shepherd.

1
01:01:28.279 --> 01:01:31.477
And the Lord said unto Moses.

2
01:01:31.517 --> 01:01:34.794
"Go. Return into Egypt."

3
01:01:34.834 --> 01:01:37.632
And Moses took his wife and his son

4
01:01:37.672 --> 01:01:40.030
and he returned to the land of Egypt.

5
01:01:40.110 --> 01:01:44.187
And Moses took the rod of God
in his hand.

6
01:01:45.666 --> 01:01:51.422
Let the ambassador from Priam.
king of Troy. approach the Pharaoh.

7
01:01:57.337 --> 01:02:01.094
Great Pharaoh. the gift of Troy
is a fabulous fabric

8
01:02:01.174 --> 01:02:03.772
from the land of the five rivers.

9
01:02:08.529 --> 01:02:12.286
Our thanks to Priam.
It is fabulous indeed.

10
01:02:12.366 --> 01:02:16.483
- It shimmers like the Nile.
- How is it made?

11
01:02:16.523 --> 01:02:20.280
No one knows.
It is spun on the looms of the gods.

12
01:02:20.320 --> 01:02:22.358
They call it silk.

13
01:02:22.398 --> 01:02:24.836
The ambassador from Jericho.

14
01:02:28.873 --> 01:02:30.992
What kingdom has sent you?

15
01:02:31.032 --> 01:02:33.790
The kingdom of the Most High.

16
01:02:43.023 --> 01:02:47.699
- What gifts do you bring?
- We bring you the word of God.

17
01:02:57.372 --> 01:02:59.331
What is this word?

18
01:02:59.371 --> 01:03:02.728
Thus sayeth the Lord God of Israel.

19
01:03:02.768 --> 01:03:05.046
"Let my people go!"

20
01:03:05.126 --> 01:03:07.724
The slaves are mine.

21
01:03:07.764 --> 01:03:12.361
Their lives are mine.
All that they own is mine.

22
01:03:14.199 --> 01:03:16.877
I do not know your God.

23
01:03:16.917 --> 01:03:19.116
nor will I let Israel go.

24
01:03:19.156 --> 01:03:23.432
Who are you to make their lives
bitter in bondage?

25
01:03:23.472 --> 01:03:27.549
Men shall be ruled by law.
not the will of other men.

26
01:03:29.348 --> 01:03:33.865
Who is this God
that I should let your people go?

27
01:03:33.905 --> 01:03:35.863
Aaron.

28
01:03:35.903 --> 01:03:39.340
Cast down my staff before Pharaoh

29
01:03:39.380 --> 01:03:42.738
that he may see the power of God.

30
01:03:44.856 --> 01:03:48.813
In this you shall know
that the Lord is God.

31
01:03:59.046 --> 01:04:03.243
Mother! He turned his staff
into a cobra!

32
01:04:07.200 --> 01:04:09.398
Nothing of HIS will harm you. my son.

33
01:04:16.033 --> 01:04:19.910
The power of your God
is a cheap magician's trick.

34
01:04:19.950 --> 01:04:21.149
Jannes.

35
01:04:38.856 --> 01:04:40.654
Mother. look!

36
01:04:47.849 --> 01:04:50.647
Jannes. do you see?

37
01:04:51.686 --> 01:04:55.363
Moses' serpent
swallows up the others.

38
01:05:03.277 --> 01:05:07.954
You gave me this staff
to rule over scorpions and serpents.

39
01:05:08.034 --> 01:05:12.031
but God made it a rod
to rule over kings.

40
01:05:12.071 --> 01:05:15.188
Hear his word. Rameses. and obey.

41
01:05:17.866 --> 01:05:19.665
Obey?

42
01:05:22.703 --> 01:05:24.661
Are there no magicians in Egypt

43
01:05:24.741 --> 01:05:28.818
that you have come back
to make serpents out of sticks?

44
01:05:28.858 --> 01:05:31.136
Or cause rabbits to appear?

45
01:05:38.371 --> 01:05:42.728
I will give your staff
a greater wonder to perform.

46
01:05:43.807 --> 01:05:46.565
Bear it before your idle people

47
01:05:46.605 --> 01:05:50.282
and bid them make bricks
without straw.

48
01:05:50.322 --> 01:05:54.359
- How can that be done?
- Let his staff provide them.

49
01:05:56.358 --> 01:06:00.035
Or let them glean straw
for themselves.

50
01:06:03.392 --> 01:06:07.149
But their tally of bricks
shall not diminish.

51
01:06:07.229 --> 01:06:11.826
So let it be written.
So let it be done.

52
01:06:39.125 --> 01:06:43.122
Aaron. Aaron. when do we leave Egypt?

53
01:06:43.162 --> 01:06:45.920
We do not leave Egypt.

54
01:06:47.239 --> 01:06:50.037
But Moses promised us.

55
01:06:50.077 --> 01:06:53.035
But you said we'd be freed!

56
01:06:54.114 --> 01:06:57.072
I have brought more evil upon you.

57
01:06:57.112 --> 01:07:02.108
God forgive my weak use
of his strength.

58
01:07:02.148 --> 01:07:05.186
Moses. what have you done to us?

59
01:07:05.266 --> 01:07:09.463
It is Pharaoh's order
that you be given no straw

60
01:07:09.542 --> 01:07:12.061
to make your tally of bricks.

61
01:07:12.101 --> 01:07:14.139
No straw?

62
01:07:14.179 --> 01:07:18.136
How can we make bricks without straw?

63
01:07:18.176 --> 01:07:21.853
You will glean the fields by night.

64
01:07:21.893 --> 01:07:24.092
Your women and children. too.

65
01:07:24.171 --> 01:07:26.370
Is this the deliverer?

66
01:07:26.410 --> 01:07:29.208
You've brought
the wrath of Pharaoh upon us!

67
01:07:29.248 --> 01:07:31.286
You put a sword in their hands!

68
01:07:31.366 --> 01:07:34.084
Stone him! Stone him!

69
01:07:42.078 --> 01:07:44.956
Stand aside! Come!

70
01:07:46.914 --> 01:07:48.953
Follow!

71
01:07:55.148 --> 01:07:59.225
There goes your deliverer.
Now go find your straw.

72
01:07:59.265 --> 01:08:03.702
Remember the tally must be the same.
Not one brick less.

73
01:08:30.961 --> 01:08:33.320
I cursed you.

74
01:08:33.399 --> 01:08:38.636
Each time Rameses took me
in his arms I cursed you. not him.

75
01:08:38.675 --> 01:08:41.314
because I love you.

76
01:08:41.353 --> 01:08:44.791
The Moses who loved you
was another man.

77
01:08:44.831 --> 01:08:47.669
No. he was not.

78
01:08:47.709 --> 01:08:51.306
You believe you've changed.
but you haven't.

79
01:08:51.346 --> 01:08:54.703
You call yourself a prophet.
a man of God.

80
01:08:54.783 --> 01:08:57.421
but I know better.

81
01:08:57.461 --> 01:09:01.458
I don't believe only the thunder
of a mountain stirs your heart.

82
01:09:01.498 --> 01:09:03.457
as you stir mine.

83
01:09:03.537 --> 01:09:08.533
Nefretiri. I have stood in the
burning light of God's own presence.

84
01:09:10.292 --> 01:09:15.208
It was not he who saved you just now.
I did that.

85
01:09:15.248 --> 01:09:18.286
Oh. Moses. Moses.

86
01:09:18.326 --> 01:09:23.682
Why. of all men. did I fall in love
with the prince of fools?

87
01:09:25.240 --> 01:09:30.756
But I believe anything you tell me
when I'm in your arms.

88
01:09:30.796 --> 01:09:33.234
Why must you deny me and yourself?

89
01:09:33.314 --> 01:09:35.753
Because I am bound to a God

90
01:09:35.833 --> 01:09:39.270
and to a people
and to a shepherd girl.

91
01:09:42.028 --> 01:09:46.465
A shepherd girl?
What can she be to you?

92
01:09:46.544 --> 01:09:51.381
Unless the desert sun
has dulled your senses.

93
01:09:51.461 --> 01:09:55.738
Does she...grate garlic on her skin?

94
01:09:55.818 --> 01:09:59.415
Or is it soft as mine?

95
01:09:59.455 --> 01:10:02.812
Are her lips chafed and dry
as the desert sand?

96
01:10:02.892 --> 01:10:08.168
Or are they moist and red
like a pomegranate?

97
01:10:10.007 --> 01:10:14.284
Is it the fragrance of myrrh
that scents her hair?

98
01:10:15.323 --> 01:10:18.081
Or is it the odour of sheep?

99
01:10:19.919 --> 01:10:23.677
There is a beauty beyond the senses.
Nefretiri.

100
01:10:23.757 --> 01:10:29.512
Beauty like the quiet
of green valleys and still waters.

101
01:10:29.552 --> 01:10:33.429
Beauty whose spirit
you cannot understand.

102
01:10:36.187 --> 01:10:38.386
Perhaps not.

103
01:10:40.104 --> 01:10:44.941
But beauty of the spirit
will not free your people. Moses.

104
01:10:45.021 --> 01:10:49.857
YOU will come to me
or THEY will never leave Egypt.

105
01:10:49.897 --> 01:10:54.813
The fate of Israel
is not in your hands. Nefretiri.

106
01:10:54.853 --> 01:10:59.769
Oh. isn't it?
Who else can soften Pharaoh's heart?

107
01:11:01.328 --> 01:11:04.926
Or harden it?

108
01:11:04.966 --> 01:11:06.924
Yes.

109
01:11:07.004 --> 01:11:09.122
You may be the lovely dust

110
01:11:09.202 --> 01:11:12.560
through which God
will work his purpose.

111
01:11:20.074 --> 01:11:22.352
Fill every jar with water.

112
01:11:22.432 --> 01:11:25.270
For seven days
there will be none to drink.

113
01:11:25.310 --> 01:11:29.347
- But this well has never run dry.
- And the river is high.

114
01:11:29.387 --> 01:11:32.825
- Whose word is that?
- One who knows.

115
01:11:32.865 --> 01:11:36.542
So fill your jars or go thirsty.

116
01:11:36.622 --> 01:11:41.298
- Miriam is always right.
- Yes. I'm going back for more jars.

117
01:11:44.216 --> 01:11:49.052
Yes. Joshua.
She comes to the well every day.

118
01:11:49.132 --> 01:11:51.251
Wait and you will see her.

119
01:11:59.684 --> 01:12:04.201
It is wise of Dathan
to send you to the well. Lilia.

120
01:12:04.281 --> 01:12:07.239
or he might find his water poisoned.

121
01:12:07.319 --> 01:12:10.436
They told me you were dead.

122
01:12:12.555 --> 01:12:15.832
To all I love. Joshua. I am dead.

123
01:12:18.550 --> 01:12:22.907
- Dathan?
- Yes. Dathan.

124
01:12:22.987 --> 01:12:25.865
Of your own free will?

125
01:12:25.945 --> 01:12:29.062
Of my own free will.

126
01:12:30.661 --> 01:12:34.658
You are no man's slave.
The hour of deliverance has come.

127
01:12:34.698 --> 01:12:37.336
Not for me. Joshua.

128
01:12:41.053 --> 01:12:44.091
Hail to thee. great god of the Nile!

129
01:12:44.131 --> 01:12:46.929
Thy waters are the blood of Egypt.

130
01:12:46.969 --> 01:12:50.246
Hail to thee. maker of barley.

131
01:12:50.286 --> 01:12:54.483
feeder of cattle. carrier of ships.

132
01:12:54.523 --> 01:12:57.081
greatest of all the gods.

133
01:12:57.121 --> 01:13:01.878
Pharaoh of Egypt!
You have not yet obeyed the Lord.

134
01:13:01.958 --> 01:13:04.596
Let my people go!

135
01:13:04.636 --> 01:13:06.594
The point of the sword...

136
01:13:06.634 --> 01:13:09.992
Let him rave
that men shall know him mad.

137
01:13:12.510 --> 01:13:14.468
Obey the Lord

138
01:13:14.548 --> 01:13:18.145
or he will raise his hand
against the waters of the river.

139
01:13:18.185 --> 01:13:22.542
I have come to bless the waters.
you have come to curse them.

140
01:13:22.622 --> 01:13:27.538
We will learn if a shepherd god
is stronger than the gods of Pharaoh.

141
01:13:27.618 --> 01:13:30.896
Water of life.
give drink to the desert

142
01:13:30.976 --> 01:13:33.174
and make green the meadow.

143
01:13:33.214 --> 01:13:35.572
Aaron.

144
01:13:35.612 --> 01:13:39.369
Stretch out my staff
against the waters.

145
01:13:48.682 --> 01:13:50.801
Look!

146
01:13:50.881 --> 01:13:53.479
Where he's touched the river.
it bleeds.

147
01:13:53.519 --> 01:13:55.797
The water turns to blood!

148
01:14:03.311 --> 01:14:05.590
(Woman screams)

149
01:14:05.630 --> 01:14:08.348
Blood flows from the god!

150
01:14:08.388 --> 01:14:11.066
See how it spreads.

151
01:14:13.384 --> 01:14:15.502
It IS blood!

152
01:14:22.337 --> 01:14:26.094
That you may know
the power of the Lord.

153
01:14:26.174 --> 01:14:29.132
for seven days. Egypt will thirst.

154
01:14:29.172 --> 01:14:32.849
- Seven days without water!
- Pestilence will be everywhere!

155
01:14:32.889 --> 01:14:35.447
Were it seven times seven days.

156
01:14:35.487 --> 01:14:39.564
no magician's trick
will set your people free.

157
01:14:44.321 --> 01:14:49.077
Sacred water. make pure the flood
from which you came.

158
01:14:59.589 --> 01:15:03.786
And God smote the land
with all manner of plagues.

159
01:15:03.826 --> 01:15:06.784
but still Pharaoh's heart
was hardened.
